      },
      "message": "fix(ui): one locked, shared GPU device for the trace test binaries\n\ntrace_composite and trace_parity made a wgpu device in each test, on\nparallel test threads, with no lock. A hybrid-GPU Windows laptop ended\nboth binaries with 0xC0000005.\n\n- headless_gpu now holds the process GPU lock (gpu_guard) and a new\n  test_gpu(suite): it takes the lock and gives the one device of the\n  process, made once and never dropped.\n- The two trace binaries and the view_pass lib test use test_gpu.\n- The three ignored evidence renderers take gpu_guard() first.\n- egui_app::gpu_test_lock re-exports the lock, so lib tests and the\n  shared device take the same one.\n\nPins: devices_asked_from_many_threads_are_one_device_used_one_at_a_time,\nthe_trace_binaries_share_one_locked_device, every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock.\n\nRefs #3379\nFixes #3605\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
